   "text": {
    "L1": "A fraction names equal parts of one whole.",
    "L2": "The bottom number tells how many equal parts make the whole, and the top number tells how many we take.",
    "L3": "Here, one-half has two equal parts, while one-quarter has four equal parts.",
    "L4": "More equal parts make smaller pieces, so one-half is bigger than one-quarter.",
    "L5": "That busts the myth that a bigger bottom number makes a bigger fraction.",
    "L6": "A fraction of a collection also means sharing the collection into equal groups.",
    "L7": "To find one-third of 15 pencils, share them into three equal groups.",
    "L8": "Each group has 5 pencils, so one-third of 15 is 5."
   },
